# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT: stylo's own tokenizer (txt.to.words / load.corpus.and.parse)
# only lower-cases text - it does NOT strip Greek polytonic diacritics
# (breathing marks, accents, iota subscript, etc.). Our stop-word list below
# is written in unaccented (monotonic-equivalent) Greek. If we hand accented
# source texts straight to stylo() and pass this list as `stop.words`, the
# literal string match inside delete.stop.words() fails silently for almost
# every accented token (e.g. "καὶ" != "και"), so the stop words barely get
# removed and MFW slots get polluted with inflected stop-word variants -
# this was the cause of the weaker/muddier heatmap.
#
# Fix: normalize (accent-fold) the corpus files ourselves BEFORE stylo ever
# reads them, so its own tokenizer only ever sees monotonic-equivalent Greek
# that matches this stop-word list exactly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

